pi.github.com/repos/sematic-ai/sematic/commits/53f67dfe4b86237f58c3f0bbe29f8f23f09aa117", "html_url": "https://github.com/sematic-ai/sematic/commit/53f67dfe4b86237f58c3f0bbe29f8f23f09aa117"}]}, {"sha": "2427c62bb9f0ab1b39f21e11e034f761ea70cd63", "node_id": "C_kwDOHNB9stoAKDI0MjdjNjJiYjlmMGFiMWIzOWYyMWUxMWUwMzRmNzYxZWE3MGNkNjM", "commit": {"author": {"name": "Sash Nagarkar", "email": "sashn45@gmail.com", "date": "2023-01-05T01:21:03Z"}, "committer": {"name": "GitHub", "email": "noreply@github.com", "date": "2023-01-05T01:21:03Z"}, "message": "Helm chart fix and refactor (#351)\n\nAside from several minor cosmetic fixes and build/test failure fixes,\r\nthe larger changes here are:\r\n\r\n* Remove kube backward compatibility checks since we only support kube\r\n>= 1.21 anyway.\r\n* Specify the sematic server image version in `Chart.yaml`, and allow\r\noverriding it from `values.yaml`. This makes versioning more explicit in\r\nthe chart publishing step, and removes the pattern of overriding an\r\noverride.\r\n* Respect the user's specified chart release name and use that for all\r\nkube objects created by the chart. This helps users track these\r\nresources more intuitively.\r\n* Moved around some of the keys in `values.yaml` to make them more\r\nexplicit and easier to understand.", "tree": {"sha": "dcc37fe1cc96689c92e98478a44370cb5058f10d", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sematic-ai/sematic/git/trees/dcc37fe1cc96689c92e98478a44370cb5058f10d"}, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sematic-ai/sematic/git/commits/2427c62bb9f0ab1b39f21e11e034f761ea70cd63", "comment_count": 0, "verification": {"verified": false, "reason": "unsigned", "signature": null, "payload": null, "verified_at": null}}, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sematic-ai/sematic/commits/2427c62bb9f0ab1b39f21e11e034f761ea70cd63", "html_url": "https://github.com/sematic-ai/sematic/commit/2427c62bb9f0ab1b39f21e11e034f761ea70cd63", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sematic-ai/sematic/commits/2